Z||000063||Will||07-06-2001||10:11 PM||||Sit down for this one:<P>'88 chassis, seam welded.<BR>Twin Turbo intercooled MY 2000 or later Northstar with LS6 controller running 15 lbs of boost (~600 rwhp, ~600 rwtq). Oil/water heat exchanger, partial flow oil and coolant filters. Freon assistance with the intercooler.<BR>VW racing transaxle with billet steel gears and Peloquin LSD to handle that power. TALL FD to clear 60 mph in 1st gear.<BR>Five link conversion for '88 rear suspension to put the power down.<BR>335/35ZR18 rear tires for traction.<BR>275/40ZR17 front tires to give it handling balance.<BR>IMSA notchback widebody kit from IRM to cover all that rubber.<BR>'84 decklid for extra engine compartment venting, and wingnuts on both of the side vents!!!<BR>Big-@$$ hood vents to help get rid of the heat and look like a baaaaaad mo-fo.<BR>XL UHMW front control arm bushings, rod end rear suspension link pivots for controllability.<BR>Coil overs at all four corners.<BR>Corvette front brakes at all four corners.<BR>Oil temp, Boost, IAT, AFR guages.<P><BR>Short throw stock height shifter.<P>75x2 to 6x9's in dash, 35x2 to 4x6's in B pillars, 200x1 to 8" sub in stock location.<BR>Single DIN head unit, with half height 10 band EQ also mounted in factory radio location.<P>C5 Corvette seats.<P>Anyone got 30 or 40K hangin around? I'll build you one...||||reg||1
